<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hermann II, Margrave of Baden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1060–1130</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hermann II was a member of the house of Zähringen and the first to call himself Margrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a>, in 1112, after the castle of Hohenbaden above Baden-Baden. Son of Hermann I, he inherited the margravial title and lands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/breisgau">Breisgau</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-forest">Black Forest</a>, and his descendants ruled Baden until 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hermann-ii-margrave-of-baden.jpg" alt="Hermann II, Margrave of Baden" width="320" height="498" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franz Ludwig Hermann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Ulrich_Schwarzwald_Pfarrkirche_Wandgem%C3%A4lde_F.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
